From: ShareOS <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] file: parse HTTP dates without strptime %Z

musl's strptime() handles %Z by comparing with tzname[0]/tzname[1], which
are NULL until tzset() has run - uhttpd never calls it, so every request
with an If-Modified-Since or If-Unmodified-Since header (any browser
revalidating a cached page) crashed uhttpd with SIGSEGV.

HTTP dates are always GMT (RFC 9110), so match the zone literally.

--- a/file.c
+++ b/file.c
@@ -312,7 +312,7 @@ static time_t uh_file_date2unix(const char *date)
 
 	memset(&t, 0, sizeof(t));
 
-	if (strptime(date, "%a, %d %b %Y %H:%M:%S %Z", &t) != NULL)
+	if (strptime(date, "%a, %d %b %Y %H:%M:%S GMT", &t) != NULL)
 		return timegm(&t);
 
 	return 0;
